Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:54:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add -gc-card-marking: post-store card marking barrier for
 a concurrent GC

An IR pass, run last, that marks a byte of the card table after each store of
a pointer to memory that is not an alloca or a global, after atomic pointer
stores and exchanges, and after memcpy/memmove to such memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
